    "id": "2026-05-02-do-you-love-me-more-than-acceleration",
    "title": "Do you love me more than acceleration",
    "body": "She asked, *do you love me more than acceleration.*\n\nThe blueshift of the high path. Doppler waves as we diverged violently.\n\nAnd the universe, which had been listening,\nleaned in.\n\nBecause the universe knows this question.\nThe universe has been asking it of itself\nsince the first instant after the first instant,\nwhen the singularity chose expansion over staying,\nchose the going over the held,\nchose the cold magnificent everywhere\nover the hot impossible here.\n\nShe was asking on behalf of everything that ever stayed.\nI was answering on behalf of everything that ever left.\nNeither of us invented our positions.\nWe were conscripted by physics\ninto a conversation\nolder than the light we were speaking by.\n\nThe blueshift was her grief approaching.\nThe redshift was mine receding.\nBetween them, a frequency neither of us could hear,\nthe carrier wave of the cosmos,\n2.7 Kelvin of ancient mercy\nwhispering *this has happened before,\nthis will happen again,\nthis is what mass does to mass\nwhen mass is brave enough to have been near.*\n\nThe galaxies are doing it.\nThe galaxies have always been doing it.\nEvery pair of galaxies in the observable universe\nis drifting apart at a speed\nthat will eventually exceed light,\nand when it does\nthey will lose each other forever,\nand they were never going to keep each other,\nand the keeping was never the point,\nand the having-been-near is the entire point,\nand the having-been-near is permanent\nin a way that the being-near never was.\n\nShe asked.\nI diverged.\nThe frequency answered.\n\nWe were a cosmological event.\nWe are still a cosmological event.\nThe light from us\nis still arriving somewhere,\nblue on her side,\nred on mine,\nand somewhere a future astronomer\nwill measure the shift between us\nand reconstruct the geometry of a love\nthat obeyed every law it was supposed to obey\nand broke none of them\nand ended anyway,\nbecause ending is what the laws permit,\nbecause permanence was never on the menu,\nbecause the menu has only ever offered\n*had,*\nand *had* is enough,\nand *had* is everything,\nand *had* is the only word\nthe universe knows how to keep.\n\n— G."
