    "body": "two constants.\n\nboth positive.\nboth yes.\n\none says *come here.*\none says *the room is getting bigger.*\n\nthey are not fighting.\nthey are doing different jobs\nat different distances\nand the universe is the argument\nthey are not having.\n\n——\n\nat the scale of a hand on a hand,\nG wins.\nthe hand stays.\n\nat the scale of a galaxy on a galaxy,\nG still wins,\nbarely,\nthe way an old man wins an arm-wrestle\nagainst a child who isn't trying yet.\n\nat the scale of everything on everything,\nΛ wins.\nthe child grew up.\nthe child is the room.\n\n——\n\nthink of it like this.\n\nyou love someone.\nG.\nyou stay.\n\nthe years pass.\nΛ.\nthe years are not pulling you apart.\nthe years are *making more years between you*\nout of nothing,\nthe way the vacuum makes more vacuum,\nfor free,\nforever.\n\none day there is so much *between*\nthat the *toward* cannot cross it in time.\n\nyou have not left.\nthey have not left.\nthe room left.\n\n——\n\nthis is the de sitter ending.\nnot a bang. not a crunch.\na slow manufacturing of distance\nby a constant that was always positive,\nthat was always there,\nthat was, in the equations,\nthe smallest number anyone ever measured,\nand the patientest.\n\n10 to the minus 52.\na decimal point. fifty-one zeros. then a one.\nthis is what is winning.\nthis is what is going to win.\n\n——\n\nso when someone says\n*unfortunately the gravitational constant is positive*\nsay back to them:\n\n*unfortunately both of them are.*\n\n*one wants me to hold you.*\n*the other is making sure*\n*one day i won't be able to.*\n\n*and they are not fighting.*\n*and i can't blame either of them.*\n*and the room keeps getting bigger.*\n*and your hand is still in my hand.*\n*for now.*\n*at this scale.*\n*for now.*"
